                  %h2#theorems Theorems
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diaconescu%27s+theorem"} Diaconescu's theorem
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/topos+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#posites Posites
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#ideals_and_sheaves"} Ideals and sheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#interpretations"} Interpretations
              %li
                %a{:href => "#examples"} Examples
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#using_ideals"} Using ideals
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#using_sheaves"} Using sheaves
              %li
                %a{:href => "#use_in_predicative_mathematics"} Use in predicative mathematics
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em posite
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,1)
                \-site
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                \-site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            of the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            (which may also be called a
            = succeed "-site" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "-site)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorifications"} categorifications
            thereof, see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-site"} 2-site
          %p
            Just as a site is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            = succeed "-valued)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            form a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            with a coverage, whose
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,1)
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+topos"} localic topos
          %p
            As locale theory serves as an approach to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            in which locales take the role traditionally held by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+bases"} topological bases
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+topology"} formal topology
            may be generated by a posite equipped with a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positivity+predicate"} positivity predicate
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_posite Definition (posite)
            %p
              A
              %strong posite
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              whose underlying category is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+category"} thin
          %p
            In other words, a posite is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            (or more generally a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preordered+set"} preordered set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            or a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
          %p The definition of coverage may be simplified a little in this case.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_coverage_on_a_poset Definition (coverage on a poset)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be a poset (or proset). A
              %strong coverage
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lhd
              between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
              that satisfies these conditions:
            %ul
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \leq u
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' \leq u
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' \lhd V'
                for some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
                such that, for every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                        %mo ′
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' \in V'
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' \leq v
            %p
              Then a
              %strong posite
              is precisely a poset (or proset) equipped with a coverage.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet-semilattice"} meet-semilattice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            have
            %em all
            finitary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meets"} meets
            but only
            %em
              %span.newWikiWord
                bounded
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/bounded+meet"} ?
            ones. That is, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ,
                  %mi w
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v, w \leq u
            for some fixed
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \wedge w
            must exist, but not otherwise. Such a poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a semilattice if and only if it has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top+element"} top element
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+category"} locally cartesian category
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_cartesian_coverage_on_a_locally_cartesian_posite Definition (cartesian coverage on a locally cartesian posite)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              be a poset (or proset) with all bounded binary meets. A
              %strong cartesian coverage
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+relation"} binary relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊲
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lhd
              between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
              that satisfies these conditions:
            %ul
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \leq u
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' \leq u
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ⊲
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi u
                        %mo ′
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' \lhd \{ v \wedge u' \;|\; v \in V \}
            %p
              Then a
              %strong locally cartesian posite
              is such a poset (or proset) equipped with such a coverage.
          %p It is a theorem that every posite whose underlying poset has all bounded binary meets is equivalent (in the sense that there is an isomorphism of sites as defined below) to a locally cartesian posite.
          %p
            In any case, given an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⊲
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V ,
          %p
            then we say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            %strong
              basic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_morphism_of_posites Definition (morphism of posites)
            %p
              Given two posites
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %strong morphism of posites
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon S \to T
              such that:
            %ul
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \leq v
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(u) \leq f(v)
                in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %li
                Given any
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \leq f(v)
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \leq f(u), f(v)
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi u
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq u, v
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi w
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \leq f(x)
              %li
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ⊲
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊲
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(u) \lhd \{ f(v) \;|\; v \in V \}
          %p
            Clauses (1–3) simply state that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            are semilattices, we can replace this with the requirement that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            preserves meets (including the top element). Clause (4) requires
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to respect covers.
          %h2#ideals_and_sheaves Ideals and sheaves
          %p
            One often looks at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_ideal Definition (ideal)
            %p
              Given a posite
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %strong ideal
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              (also called a
              = succeed ";" do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,1)
                  \-sheaf
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaf"} sheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              satisfying these conditions:
            %ol
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \leq v
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in I
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in I
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⊲
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \subseteq I
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \in I
          %p
            In other words, it is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            valued in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
            (rather than in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            as is the default).
          %p
            A subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            that satisfies condition (1) alone states that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            is a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+subset"} lower subset
            (a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-presheaf"} (0,1)-presheaf
          %p
            The ideals on a posite form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Id
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id(S)
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{0,1}(S)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
          %p
            Every element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            may be interpreted as an ideal on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ,
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u,v
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            belongs to the
            %strong
              ideal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/represented+functor"} represented
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            if and only if
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \leq v
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            represents its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/down+set"} down set
          %p
            The frame of ideals is given by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is a frame, we make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            into a posite using its canonical coverage (see the examples below). Then the operation from elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to ideals on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a morphism of posites; furthermore, given any morphism of posites from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to a frame
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            (with its canonical coverage), there exists a unique frame
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Id
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id(S)
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            that makes the obvious triangle commute.
          %p
            If instead we treat a posite as a special kind of site and look at its
            = succeed "-sheaves," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+of+sheaves"} topos of sheaves
              on any posite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localic+topos"} localic topos
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is obvious if we use the definition of “localic topos” which says that it is generated by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subterminal+objects"} subterminal objects
          %p The relevant locale is precisely the locale of ideals.
          %h2#interpretations Interpretations
          %p
            Given a posite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            as
            %strong basic opens
            of a space which is generated from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            using its coverage, to produce a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            %strong base
            for a locale. See the example coming from a topological space below to see how this can work precisely for a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+locale"} topological locale
          %p
            A coverage can be seen as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequent"} sequent
            calculus; the interpretation of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⊲
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
          %p in topology is analogous to the interpretation of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \vdash Q
          %p
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjunction"} disjunctively
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                intuitionistic sequent
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/intuitionistic+sequent"} ?
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#using_ideals Using ideals
          %p
            Any poset (or proset)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coverage"} canonical coverage
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊲
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
              if and only if, for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' \leq u
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u'
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
              of some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
              such that, for every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' \in V'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v \in V
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi v
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v' \leq v
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊲
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              is a join of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            and then the canonical coverage is cartesian. In this case,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Id
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id(S)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            itself. (Analogously, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            with its canonical coverage, then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(E)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+of+sheaves"} topos of sheaves
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+base"} topological base
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a semilattice under
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            into a posite by defining
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊲
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \lhd V
              if and only if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (which is not necessarily the same as a join in
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            The frame generated by this posite is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+of+opens"} frame of opens
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+space"} sober space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale+of+real+numbers"} locale of real numbers
            is generated from the locally cartesian poset
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \coloneqq \mathbb{Q}^op \times \mathbb{Q}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            is the usual poset of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊲
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y) \lhd \empty
              whenever
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \geq y
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w,z) \lhd \{(w,x),(y,z)\}
              whenever
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi y
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \leq y \lt x \leq z
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi w
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w,z) \lhd \{ (x,y) \;|\; w \lt x \lt y \lt z \}
              \.
          %p
            Often you will see
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm\infty
            added to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            in a description of this locale, which adds a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top+element"} top element
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and so makes it into a semilattice, but that makes no difference to the generated locale in this case.
          %h3#using_sheaves Using sheaves
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation+topology"} double negation topology
            used in the sheaf-theoretic approach to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
            is a posite. More generally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} Classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set-theoretic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
            is done exclusively on posites. One “reason” for this (in the sense of a reason why set-theorists have not been forced to look beyond such models) is explained in
            %a{:href => "#Freyd"} the paper by Freyd
            below.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice+of+commutative+subalgebras"} semilattice of commutative subalgebras
            of a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+algebra"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a posite (with trivial topology) internal to whose sheaf topos we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+Gelfand+duality+theorem"} constructive Gelfand duality theorem
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            was externally non-commutative.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+logic"} propositional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+theory"} geometric theory
            is localic, and can be presented as sheaves on a posite of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
          %h2#use_in_predicative_mathematics Use in predicative mathematics
          %p
            We call a frame (or locale)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %strong accessible
            if it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Id
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id(S)
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            posite
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            with its canonical coverage.) Since many predicativists have philosophical objections to working with large objects at all, they may prefer to work with small posites directly. Whatever the philosophy, we may use small posites in place of accessible locales, or at any rate use this to prove that the category of the latter is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+moderate+category"} essentially moderate
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+topology"} Formal topology
            is a programme for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            which is based on using small posites. However, formal topologists also require a positivity predicate on their posites; the intended interpretation is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            is positive iff its corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspace"} open subspace
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+space"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+spaces"} compact spaces
            (and related notions) in a predicative constructive framework.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              Most of this article is based on
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stone+Spaces"} Stone Spaces
          %p
            On
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
          %ul#Freyd
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"}> Peter Freyd
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em All topoi are localic or why permutation models prevail
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/13480/set-theoretic-forcing-over-sites"} This MO question
              and its answer.
